x Attack Leaks Data From Air-Gapped Systems via Video Cable Emissions](https://thehackernews.com/2026/07/new-trojpix-attack-leaks-data-from-air.html)\n  - [ ] [New Java-Based QuimaRAT MaaS Built to Run on Windows, Linux, and macOS](https://thehackernews.com/2026/07/new-java-based-quimarat-maas-built-to.html)\n  - [ ] [Opera GX Flaw Let Malicious Sites Auto-Install Mods to Steal Data From Visited Pages](https://thehackernews.com/2026/07/opera-gx-flaw-let-malicious-sites-auto.html)\n  - [ ] [SkillCloak Lets Malicious AI Agent Skills Evade Static Scanners with Self-Extracting Packing](https://thehackernews.com/2026/07/new-skillcloak-technique-lets-malicious.html)\n- Security Affairs\n  - [ ] [Adobe ColdFusion flaw CVE-2026-48282 now exploited in the wild](https://securityaffairs.com/194837/hacking/adobe-coldfusion-flaw-cve-2026-48282-now-exploited-in-the-wild.html)\n  - [ ] [Hidden Web Prompts Trick AI Agents Into Sending Money](https://securityaffairs.com/194822/ai/hidden-web-prompts-trick-ai-agents-into-sending-money.html)\n  - [ ] [Seven Bugs in FatFs Put IoT and Embedded Devices at Risk](https://securityaffairs.com/194808/security/seven-bugs-in-fatfs-put-iot-and-embedded-devices-at-risk.html)\n  - [ ] [Bad Epoll Flaw Gives Attackers Root Access on Linux and Android](https://securityaffairs.com/194795/hacking/bad-epoll-flaw-gives-attackers-root-access-on-linux-and-android.html)\n- Security Weekly Podcast Network (Audio)\n  - [ ] [Mastering agent permissions and Identiverse interviews - Howard Ting, Ajay Gupta, Sandy Bird, Amir Ofek - ESW #466](http://sites.libsyn.com/18678/mastering-agent-permissions-and-identiverse-interviews-howard-ting-ajay-gupta-sandy-bird-amir-ofek-esw-466)\n- 吾爱破解论坛\n  - [ ] [基于文本匹配的VMP还原思路](https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s?__biz=MjM5Mjc3MDM2Mw==&mid=2651144621&idx=1&sn=69ef8eb1d2d840cfab3b6b1e61a7e196)\n- 网安寻路人\n  - [ ] [AI智能体的系统架构与安全治理：从输出风险到行动风险](https://mp.weixin.qq.com/s?__biz=MzIxODM0NDU4MQ==&mid=2247508643&idx=1&sn=c33c8a8ed4451345dd9d2609420cf79c)\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BruceFeIix/picker/issues/2546/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/BruceFeIix/picker/issues/2546/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2786","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2786/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2786/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2786/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2786","id":4195438556,"node_id":"I_kwDORGgqa876EU_c","number":2786,"title":"[ONBOARD: 2 RTC] Compare RustChain to Another Blockchain Project","user":{"login":"Scottcjn","id":121303252,"node_id":"U_kgDOBzrw1A","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/121303252?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn","html_url":"https://github.com/Scottcjn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Scottcjn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":10115029430,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACWucZtg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/good%20first%20issue","name":"good first issue","color":"7057ff","default":true,"description":"Good for newcomers"},{"id":10115035859,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACWucy0w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/bounty","name":"bounty","color":"0E8A16","default":false,"description":"RTC-paid bounty"},{"id":10153071106,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACXSuSAg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/community","name":"community","color":"5319E7","default":false,"description":"Community engagement"},{"id":10360962887,"node_id":"LA_kwDORGgqa88AAAACaY-_Rw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/labels/onboarding","name":"onboarding","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":625,"created_at":"2026-04-02T15:42:09Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T05:03:23Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Bounty: 3 RTC\n\n### What You'll Do\nResearch RustChain and compare it to another blockchain project you know.\n\n### Steps\n1. **Pick any other blockchain project**: Bitcoin, Ethereum, Solana, Ergo, Chia, whatever you know\n2. **Write a comparison** (300-800 words) covering:\n   - Consensus mechanism differences (PoW vs PoS vs PoA vs RustChain's Proof of Antiquity)\n   - Hardware requirements\n   - Environmental approach\n   - Community model\n   - What each project does better\n3. **Post as a comment here**\n\n### What Counts\n- Must show you actually read about both projects\n- Honest comparison, it's fine to say where RustChain falls short\n- We learn from your outside perspective\n- Tables/charts welcome but not required\n\n### Payment\n3 RTC for a thoughtful, accurate comparison.\n\n**Difficulty**: Easy-Medium | **Time**: 30-45 min | **Skills**: Research, writing\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2786/reactions","total_count":14,"+1":7,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":2,"confused":0,"heart":1,"rocket":3,"eyes":1},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Scottcjn/rustchain-bounties/issues/2786/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qojulia/QuantumOptics.jl/issues/407","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qojulia/QuantumOptics.jl","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qojulia/QuantumOptics.jl/issues/407/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qojulia/QuantumOptics.jl/issues/407/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qojulia/QuantumOptics.jl/issues/407/events","html_url":"https://github.com/qojulia/QuantumOptics.jl/issues/407","id":2442495188,"node_id":"I_kwDOAzkJ986RlYTU","number":407,"title":"Update the benchmark suite and bring it into the CI runner [$400]","user":{"login":"Krastanov","id":705248,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwNTI0OA==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/705248?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov","html_url":"https://github.com/Krastanov","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Krastanov/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":7277527310,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAzkJ988AAAABscZBDg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qojulia/QuantumOptics.jl/labels/bug%20bounty","name":"bug bounty","color":"D7B4F0","default":false,"description":"There is an award for solving this issue."},{"id":7277528655,"node_id":"LA_kwDOAzkJ988AAAABscZGTw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qojulia/QuantumOptics.jl/labels/bounty:400","name":"bounty:400","color":"FABF75","default":false,"description":""}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":7,"created_at":"2024-08-01T13:37:33Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T04:45:24Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"<details>\r\n<summary><strong>Bug bounty logistic details</strong> (click to expand)</summary>\r\n\r\nTo claim exclusive time to work on this bounty either post a comment here or message [skrastanov@umass.edu](mailto:skrastanov@umass.edu) with:\r\n\r\n- your name\r\n- github username\r\n- **(optional)** a brief list of previous pertinent projects you have engaged in\r\n\r\nCurrently the project is claimed by `no one` until `...`.\r\n\r\nIf you want to, you can work on this project without making a claim, however claims are encouraged to give you and other contributors peace of mind. Whoever has made a claim takes precedence when solutions are considered.\r\n\r\nYou can always propose your own funded project, if you would like to contribute something of value that is not yet covered by an official bounty.\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n# Update the benchmark suite and bring it into the CI runner [$400]\r\n\r\nQuantumOptics.jl has an in-depth benchmarking suite that has bitrotted in the last few years. To claim this bounty:\r\n\r\n- Set up a benchmark-on-CI infrastructure (e.g. similar to the one in QuantumClifford.jl) that runs QuantumOptics-specific benchmarks on each pull request\r\n- Include all old benchmarks in that infrastructure (reusing the existing benchmark suite as much as possible) and make it easy to add new micro-benchmarks as new features get developed.\r\n\r\nThe above are for the sake of the developers of this package. However, this bounty also requires the following to be done for the sake of users:\r\n\r\n- Fix up the capability to run benchmarks in comparison to popular python packages (qutip) and add comparative Julia packages (QuantumToolbox.jl)\r\n- Create a makefile that let's a developer to easily update the webpage presenting these comparative benchmarks to the user.\r\n\r\n**Required skills**: Understanding of Julia's and Python's benchmarking infrastructure.\r\n\r\n**Reviewer**: Stefan Krastanov and/or @david-pl \r\n\r\n**Duration**: 2 months\r\n\r\n#### Payout procedure:\r\n\r\nThe Funding for these bounties comes from the National Science Foundation and from the NSF Center for Quantum Networks. The payouts are managed by the NumFOCUS foundation and processed in bulk once every two months. If you live in a country in which NumFOCUS can make payments, you can participate in this bounty program.\r\n\r\n[Click here for more details about the bug bounty program.](https://github.com/QuantumSavory/.github/blob/main/BUG_BOUNTIES.md)","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qojulia/QuantumOptics.jl/issues/407/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/qojulia/QuantumOptics.jl/issues/407/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zaproxy/zaproxy/issues/9377","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zaproxy/zaproxy","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zaproxy/zaproxy/issues/9377/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zaproxy/zaproxy/issues/9377/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zaproxy/zaproxy/issues/9377/events","html_url":"https://github.com/zaproxy/zaproxy/issues/9377","id":4825275259,"node_id":"I_kwDOAjHKnc8AAAABH5vbew","number":9377,"title":"Add-on submission: Disclosure Contact Lookup (disclose/zap-lookup)","user":{"login":"yesnet0","id":12779999,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyNzc5OTk5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12779999?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/yesnet0","html_url":"https://github.com/yesnet0","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yesnet0/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yesnet0/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yesnet0/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yesnet0/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yesnet0/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yesnet0/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yesnet0/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yesnet0/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/yesnet0/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-07-07T04:37:51Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T04:37:51Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Submitting a new third-party add-on for the ZAP Marketplace.\n\n### Add-on repo\nhttps://github.com/disclose/zap-lookup\n\n### Your contact details\nhello@disclose.io — a [disclose.io](https://disclose.io) project (an open, vendor-neutral nonprofit for vulnerability disclosure).\n\n### Are you one of the authors?\nYes.\n\n### License\nMIT (see `LICENSE`).\n\n### Build instructions\n`gradle jarZapAddOn` (JDK 17, Gradle 8.13+). CI builds the `.zap` on every push (`.github/workflows/build.yml`), and a prebuilt `.zap` is attached to the [v1.0.0 release](https://github.com/disclose/zap-lookup/releases/tag/v1.0.0).\n\n### Link for more information\n- Repo / README: https://github.com/disclose/zap-lookup\n- The attribution API it calls: https://lookup.disclose.io\n\n### What it does\n**Disclosure Contact Lookup** adds a right-click **“Find disclosure contact”** menu item on any HTTP message. It resolves the selected host to its owning organization and a ranked list of security-disclosure channels (security.txt, VDP / bug-bounty programs, PSIRT directories) via the free [lookup.disclose.io](https://lookup.disclose.io) attribution API — so a tester knows exactly where to report a finding. It’s the open-source-proxy sibling of the disclose.io Burp and Caido extensions.\n\n**Privacy / safety:** it sends only the *host string* (e.g. `github.com`) — never request/response content — and makes only that one read-only outbound call. No scan traffic, no writes.\n\n### Status\nAlpha (first release). Add-on id `zap-lookup`, package `io.disclose.zaplookup`, min ZAP version 2.16.0. Verified: builds in CI, and loads cleanly in ZAP 2.17.0 (the extension initializes with no errors).\n\n### Promote to Beta or Release?\nNo — start at Alpha.\n\n### Anything else we should know?\nHappy to add an integrated help file or address any review feedback.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zaproxy/zaproxy/issues/9377/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zaproxy/zaproxy/issues/9377/timeline","performed_via_github_app":n