w","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zhangjiayang6835-cyber/ai-research/labels/security","name":"security","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null},{"id":11378455837,"node_id":"LA_kwDOTGNm188AAAACpjV1HQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zhangjiayang6835-cyber/ai-research/labels/expert","name":"expert","color":"ededed","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":4,"created_at":"2026-07-07T00:00:21Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T00:41:30Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## 🐛 Bug Bounty: Remote Code Execution via Unsafe Pickle Deserialization\n\n**难度:** Expert | **奖励:** $100 USD\n\n### 漏洞描述\n此漏洞描述了一个常见的安全问题: Remote Code Execution via Unsafe Pickle Deserialization。需要提交修复代码。\n\n### 提交要求\n- 提交修复代码（Python/JavaScript）\n- 在 issue 评论中以代码块形式提交\n- 也可以创建 Pull Request\n\n### 评估标准\n- 代码正确修复了安全漏洞\n- 没有引入新的安全问题\n- 代码简洁且有效\n\n---\n*任务由 Daily Task Generator 自动创建*","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zhangjiayang6835-cyber/ai-research/issues/615/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zhangjiayang6835-cyber/ai-research/issues/615/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/25378","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/25378/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/25378/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/25378/events","html_url":"https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/25378","id":4824081346,"node_id":"I_kwDOJH_K4M8AAAABH4mjwg","number":25378,"title":"Python GGUF parser (gguf_reader.py) lacks dimension validation present in C++ parser — DoS / crash on malicious model files","user":{"login":"Arielpoghon","id":183567726,"node_id":"U_kgDOCvEFbg","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/183567726?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arielpoghon","html_url":"https://github.com/Arielpoghon","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arielpoghon/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arielpoghon/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arielpoghon/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arielpoghon/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arielpoghon/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arielpoghon/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arielpoghon/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arielpoghon/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Arielpoghon/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-07-07T00:11:33Z","updated_at":"2026-07-07T00:11:33Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Summary\n\nThe Python GGUF reader (`gguf-py/gguf/gguf_reader.py`) is missing input validation that exists in the C++ parser, making it vulnerable to DoS and crashes from crafted model files.\n\n## Bug 1 — Missing `n_dims` upper bound (`gguf_reader.py` ~L267–271)\n\nIn `_get_tensor_info_field`, `n_dims` is read as `uint32` with **no upper-bound check against `GGML_MAX_DIMS` (4)**, unlike the C++ parser:\n\n```python\nn_dims = self._get(offs, np.uint32)\n...\ndims = self._get(offs, np.uint64, n_dims[0])\n```\n\n- A crafted file with `n_dims = 1000000` triggers an 8 MB read from the memmap (1000000 × 8 bytes), likely causing an `IndexError` crash when the file is too small — or hanging the process on large sparse files.\n- `n_dims = 0xFFFFFFFF` would attempt a ~32 GiB allocation (via the memmap view), causing an OOM kill on most systems.\n\nThe C++ parser (`llama.cpp` in `llama_model_loader`) **does** clamp `n_dims` to `GGML_MAX_DIMS` before proceeding. The Python path lacks this guard entirely.\n\n## Bug 2 — Integer overflow in `np.prod()` (`gguf_reader.py` ~L329–340)\n\nIn `_build_tensors`, total element count is computed as:\n\n```python\nn_elems = int(np.prod(dims))\n```\n\n`dims` is of type `np.uint64`, so `np.prod` wraps silently on overflow (modulo 2^64).\n\n**Example:** `dims = [4194305, 4194305, 211106198978564]`\nActual product ≈ 3.7 × 10^27, but `np.prod` returns **4** due to wraparound.\n\nThis causes:\n- An undersized `memmap` read (`item_count` is far too small)\n- A subsequent `reshape(np_dims)` crash because the total element count doesn't match the shape\n\nAn attacker can craft a GGUF file that passes through the parser, triggers the overflow, and crashes any tool using the Python reader (e.g. `convert.py`, `scripts/`, or third-party GGUF consumers).\n\n---\n\nBoth were reported to huntr.com (Protect AI's AI/ML bug bounty platform) and are awaiting validation. Flagging here directly since the Python parser is a separate implementation from the already-patched C++ parser (CVE-2026-33298), which does not cover this code path.\n\n**Can a maintainer confirm these are still present and unaddressed?**\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/25378/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ggml-org/llama.cpp/issues/25378/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zhangjiayang6835-cyber/ai-research/issues/604","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zhangjiayang6835-cyber/ai-research","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zhangjiayang6835-cyber/ai-research/issues/604/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zhangjiayang6835-cyber/ai-research/issues/604/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/zhangjiayang6835-cyber/ai-research/issues/604/events","html_url":"https://github.com/zhangjiayang6835-cyber/ai-research/issues/604","id":4824030113,"node_id":"I_kwDOTGNm188AAAABH4jboQ","number":604,"title":"[BUG] WebAssembly Memory Corruption → Sandbox Escape $100","user":{"login":"zhangjiayang6835-cyber","id":288065324,"node_id":"U_kgDOESuHLA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/288065324?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/zhangjiayang6835-cyber","html_url":"https://github.com/zhangjiayang6835-cyber","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zhangjiayang6835-cyber/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zhangjiayang6835-cyber/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zhangjiayang6835-cyber/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zhangjiayang6835-cyber/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zhangjiayang6835-cyber/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zhangjiayang6835-cyber/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zhangjiayang6835-cyber/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zhangjiayang6835-cyber/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/zhangjiayang6835-cyber/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":11346812202,"node_id":"LA_kwDOTGNm