cureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/10966)\n- **Repository:** [SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty](https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty)\n- **Comments:** 0\n- **Last Updated:** 2026-07-06T21:42:49Z\n\n#### 3. [[Bounty] Help fix broken file upload component in React/TypeScript (.tsx) bounty bounty:15](https://github.com/Hazyshades/Sendly-Test-Repo/issues/41)\n- **Repository:** [Hazyshades/Sendly-Test-Repo](https://github.com/Hazyshades/Sendly-Test-Repo)\n- **Comments:** 6\n- **Last Updated:** 2026-07-06T21:33:20Z\n\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dev-kp-eloper/BountyScout/issues/399/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dev-kp-eloper/BountyScout/issues/399/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mswell/bountybrain/issues/1","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mswell/bountybrain","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mswell/bountybrain/issues/1/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mswell/bountybrain/issues/1/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mswell/bountybrain/issues/1/events","html_url":"https://github.com/mswell/bountybrain/issues/1","id":4815615831,"node_id":"I_kwDOTOul5c8AAAABHwh3Vw","number":1,"title":"PRD: BountyBrain — MCP multi-plataforma de bug bounty (HackerOne + YesWeHack, read-only)","user":{"login":"mswell","id":2567185,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjI1NjcxODU=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2567185?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mswell","html_url":"https://github.com/mswell","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mswell/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mswell/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mswell/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mswell/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mswell/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mswell/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mswell/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mswell/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mswell/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":11429255300,"node_id":"LA_kwDOTOul5c8AAAACqTyYhA","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mswell/bountybrain/labels/ready-for-agent","name":"ready-for-agent","color":"0E8A16","default":false,"description":"PRD/issue synthesized and ready for an AFK coding agent"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2026-07-06T03:06:02Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T21:58:49Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Problem Statement\n\nPesquisadores de bug bounty que trabalham em múltiplas plataformas (HackerOne, YesWeHack, Bugcrowd, Intigriti) não têm um jeito de dar a um agente de IA memória persistente e consultável sobre seus programas, scopes e histórico pessoal de reports recompensados. Existe o `H1Brain`, um MCP que resolve isso só para HackerOne (sync de programas/scopes/reports pessoais em SQLite + briefing de ataque via `hack(handle)`). Não existe equivalente maduro para as outras plataformas, e as ferramentas existentes (`bbscope`, `bounty-targets-data`, `rix4uni/scope`) resolvem apenas scope público agregado — sem conta autenticada, sem histórico pessoal, sem briefing.\n\n## Solution\n\nConstruir o **BountyBrain**: um MCP server (TypeScript) + skill companion, read-only, que sincroniza programas/scopes/reports pessoais recompensados de múltiplas plataformas de bug bounty num schema SQLite unificado, e expõe tools consultáveis (incluindo uma tool de briefing `hack(platform, handle)`) para qualquer client MCP (Pi, Claude Code, Claude Desktop). MVP cobre HackerOne primeiro (API estável, PAT), depois YesWeHack (Bearer token manual, sem automação de login). Bugcrowd e Intigriti ficam como adapters futuros. Nenhuma ação de escrita em nenhuma plataforma, em nenhuma fase.\n\n## User Stories\n\n1. Como pesquisador de bug bounty, quero sincronizar meus programas acessíveis no HackerOne para o banco local, para não precisar consultar a plataforma manualmente toda vez.\n2. Como pesquisador, quero sincronizar os scopes (in-scope/out-of-scope) de um programa HackerOne específico, para saber rapidamente o que posso ou não testar.\n3. Como pesquisador, quero sincronizar meus reports pessoais recompensados no HackerOne, para ter histórico local pesquisável.\n4. Como pesquisador, quero buscar programas por nome/handle/plataforma (`search_programs`), para encontrar rapidamente um programa sem abrir o navegador.\n5. Como pesquisador, quero buscar assets em escopo por domínio/tipo/plataforma (`search_scopes`), para saber se um asset específico está elegível a bounty em qualquer plataforma sincronizada.\n6. Como pesquisador, quero buscar meus reports passados por peso/severidade/programa/plataforma (`search_reports`), para relembrar o que já encontrei e onde.\n7. Como pesquisador, quero rodar `hack(platform, handle)` e receber um briefing com scope atual + meu histórico de findings naquele programa, para começar uma sessão de hacking com contexto real em vez de do zero.\n8. Como pesquisador, quero que a busca (`search_programs`/`search_scopes`/`search_reports`) funcione cross-platform quando eu não especificar `platform`, para comparar oportunidades entre HackerOne e YesWeHack sem trocar de ferramenta.\n9. Como pesquisador, quero configurar minha autenticação do HackerOne (username + PAT) num único arquivo local, para não espalhar segredos em vários lugares.\n10. Como pesquisador, quero configurar meu Bearer token do YesWeHack manualmente (colando um token já gerado), para não precisar guardar minha senha nem meu segredo de TOTP em disco.\n11. Como pesquisador, quero que o BountyBrain me avise claramente quando o token do YesWeHack expirar ou estiver ausente (ao invés de falhar silenciosamente ou tentar logar sozinho), para eu saber exatamente o que fazer (gerar novo token).\n12. Como pesquisador, quero uma tool `check_auth(platform)` para verificar proativamente se minhas credenciais ainda são válidas, sem precisar gastar uma chamada de negócio real para descobrir isso.\n13. Como pesquisador, quero que o sistema registre localmente quando uma verificação de auth funcionou ou falhou pela última vez, para eu (e o projeto) aprendermos o TTL real do token do YesWeHack, já que a plataforma não documenta isso publicamente.\n14. Como mantenedor do projeto, quero um schema de dados unificado entre plataformas (`programs`, `scopes`, `reports` com coluna `platform`), para que as tools de busca funcionem de forma consistente independente da plataforma de origem.\n15. Como mantenedor, quero que cada registro guarde o payload bruto original (`raw_json`), para nunca perder informação específica de uma plataforma que não caiba no schema comum.\n16. Como mantenedor, quero que tools de sincronização sejam prefixadas por plataforma (`hackerone_sync_programs`, `yeswehack_sync_scopes`, etc.), porque autenticação e paginação diferem de verdade entre plataformas e não vale a pena forçar uma abstração comum aí.\n17. Como usuário de segurança, quero ter certeza absoluta de que o BountyBrain nunca escreve, comenta ou muda status de nenhum report em nenhuma plataforma, para que ações no programa continuem sendo decisão exclusivamente minha.\n18. Como contribuidor open source, quero clonar o repositório, rodar `npm install && npm run build`, e registrar o MCP manualmente no meu client (Pi/Claude Desktop/Claude Code), sem depender de publicação no npm.\n19. Como usuário de qualquer coding agent compatível com o padrão `npx skills`, quero instalar a skill do BountyBrain (`skills/bug-bounty/bountybrain/SKILL.md`) via `npx skills add`, para usar o MCP com orientação de uso correta desde o primeiro dia.\n20. Como mantenedor, quero testes unitários com mocks das APIs do HackerOne/YesWeHack cobrindo parsing e schema, para pegar regressões sem depender de credenciais reais em CI.\n21. Como pesquisador, quero rodar uma verificação manual real (contra a API de verdade) como checklist antes de cada release, para confirmar que os adapters ainda funcionam com a API atual das plataformas.\n22. Como mantenedor, quero que uma futura base de reports públicos disclosed (equivalente ao dataset do H1Brain) seja adicionada como Fase 2 separada e opcional, sem bloquear a entrega do MVP.\n23. Como mantenedor, quero que adapters de Bugcrowd e Intigriti sejam adicionados numa fase futura, seguindo a mesma interface de adapter estabelecida por HackerOne/YesWeHack.\n\n## Implementation Decisions\n\n- **Stack:** TypeScript, usando o SDK oficial `@modelcontextprotocol/sdk`. Storage local via SQLite (`better-sqlite3`).\n- **Ordem de entrega:** adapter HackerOne completo primeiro (read-only: sync programs/scopes/reports pessoais) → adapter YesWeHack em seguida → Bugcrowd/Intigriti como adapters futuros (fora do MVP).\n- **Autenticação HackerOne:** username + Personal Access Token, lidos de `~/.config/bountybrain/secrets.env` (`HACKERONE_USERNAME`, `HACKERONE_TOKEN`).\n- **Autenticação YesWeHack:** Bearer token colado manualmente pelo usuário (`YESWEHACK_TOKEN` no mesmo arquivo). Sem automação de login (sem guardar email/senha/segredo TOTP). Detecção de expiração é reativa (`401` da API de fato) mais uma tool `check_auth(platform)` para checagem proativa. Toda verificação (sucesso ou falha) grava em uma tabela local `auth_state(platform, last_verified_at, last_failed_at, notes)` — nunca grava o token em si — para acumular dado real sobre o TTL do token, que não é documentado publicamente pela plataforma.\n- **Schema unificado** entre plataformas:\n  ```sql\n  programs(id, platform, handle, name, offers_bounties, submission_state, raw_json, synced_at)\n  scopes(id, platform, program_handle, asset_identifier, asset_type, eligible_for_bounty, eligible_for_submission, max_severity, instruction, raw_json, synced_at)\n  reports(id, platform, program_handle, title, state, severity_rating, weakness_name, weakness_cwe, bounty_amount, bounty_currency, vulnerability_information, created_at, bounty_awarded_at, disclosed_at, raw_json, synced_at)\n  auth_state(platform, last_verified_at, last_failed_at, notes)\n  ```\n  Cada tabela guarda `raw_json` do payload original da API, para preservar fidelidade quando o schema comum não capturar algum campo específico de uma plataforma.\n- **Superfície de tools MCP:**\n  - Prefixadas por plataforma (sync): `hackerone_sync_programs()`, `hackerone_sync_scopes(handle)`, `hackerone_sync_reports()`, `yeswehack_sync_programs()`, `yeswehack_sync_scopes(handle)`, `yeswehack_sync_reports()`.\n  - Unificadas (busca/briefing, `platform` opcional): `search_programs(platform?, query?, bounty_only?)`, `search_scopes(platform?, program?, asset?, bounty_only?)`, `search_reports(platform?, program?, weakness?, severity?)`, `hack(platform, handle)`, `check_auth(platform)`.\n- **Read-only por design:** nenhuma tool de escrita (comentário, mudança de status, submissão de report) existe no código em nenhuma plataforma, em nenhuma fase — não é uma flag de configuração, é ausência de código.\n- **Credenciais:** um único arquivo `~/.config/bountybrain/secrets.env`, prefixado por plataforma, permissão `600`, fora do repositório (`.gitignore`), nunca logado, nunca persistido no SQLite.\n- **Estrutura do repositório:**\n  ```text\n  bountybrain/\n  ├── LICENSE (MIT)\n  ├── PRD.md\n  ├── README.md\n  ├── package.json\n  ├── tsconfig.json\n  ├── src/\n  │   ├── server.ts\n  │   ├── db/ (schema.ts, client.ts)\n  │   └── platforms/ (hackerone.ts, yeswehack.ts, bugcrowd.ts stub, intigriti.ts stub)\n  ├── test/\n  └── skills/bug-bounty/bountybrain/SKILL.md\n  ```\n- **Skill:** vive dentro do próprio repositório, seguindo o padrão do ecossistema `npx skills` (`mattpocock/skills`), instalável via `npx skills add <owner>/bountybrain` em qualquer coding agent compatível.\n- **Distribuição:** sem publicação no npm por enquanto. Instalação via clone + `npm install && npm run build` + registro manual do MCP no client. Publicação no npm é considerada apenas quando HackerOne + YesWeHack estiverem estáveis e testados de verdade.\n- **Licença:** MIT, projeto open source desde o início.\n\n## Testing Decisions\n\n- Testes unitários com **mocks** das respostas de API do HackerOne e YesWeHack (fixtures de payload real, sem bater na API de verdade).\n- Cobertura prioritária: parsing/normalização de payload → schema unificado (garantir que campos obrigatórios nunca ficam nulos silenciosamente, que `raw_json` sempre é preservado).\n- Nenhuma credencial real (PAT/Bearer) em CI. Testes de integração real contra as APIs ficam como checklist manual de validação antes de cada release, não como pipeline automatizado — decisão explícita para não expor segredos em CI de um repositório open source.\n- Um bom teste aqui verifica comportamento observável (ex: \"dado este payload de `/programs`, `search_programs` retorna estes registros normalizados\"), não detalhes de implementação interna do adapter.\n\n## Out of Scope\n\n- Qualquer ação de escrita em qualquer plataforma (comentar report, mudar status, submeter report). Permanentemente fora de escopo, não é uma feature futura.\n- Login automatizado (email + senha + TOTP) para YesWeHack. Só Bearer token manual.\n- Base de reports públicos disclosed (equivalente aos 3.600+ reports do H1Brain) — vira Fase 2 separada, não faz parte deste PRD/MVP.\n- Adapters de Bugcrowd e Intigriti — ficam para fase futura, fora deste PRD.\n- Publicação no npm.\n- Qualquer scraping de scope público agregado sem autenticação (isso já é resolvido por `bbscope`/`bounty-targets-data`/`rix4uni/scope` e não é o objetivo deste projeto).\n- Integração com Raijū ou qualquer outro repositório/skill existente — o BountyBrain é standalone por decisão explícita.\n\n## Further Notes\n\n- Este PRD nasceu de uma sessão de alinhamento (`grilling`) com o mantenedor, cobrindo 14 decisões arquiteturais sequenciais antes de qualquer código ser escrito. O documento completo dessa sessão, incluindo o raciocínio por trás de cada decisão, está em `PRD.md` na raiz do repositório.\n- HackerOne foi escolhido como primeira plataforma por ter API pública, madura e com autenticação simples (PAT), servindo para validar a arquitetura de adapters/schema antes de lidar com a parte mais incerta (YesWeHack, cujo endpoint de auth real é `POST /login` + `POST /account/totp` retornando um Bearer de sessão sem TTL documentado — confirmado lendo o código-fonte do `bbscope`, não a documentação renderizada em JS da API).\n- O nome do pacote/binário (`bountybrain`) e a decisão de não publicar no npm ainda são revisáveis quando o projeto estabilizar — não são decisões permanentes, ao contrário das de escopo de escrita/leitura.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mswell/bountybrain/issues/1/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/mswell/bountybrain/issues/1/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/10966","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/10966/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/10966/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/10966/events","html_url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/10966","id":4823312728,"node_id":"I_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABH33pWA","number":10966,"title":"Auth endpoints should return 400 for invalid request bodies","user":{"login":"mircats98gpt","id":291542861,"node_id":"U_kgDOEWCXTQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/291542861?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mircats98gpt","html_url":"https://github.com/mircats98gpt","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mircats98gpt/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mircats98gpt/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mircats98gpt/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mircats98gpt/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mircats98gpt/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mircats98gpt/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mircats98gpt/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mircats98gpt/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mircats98gpt/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-07-06T21:42:49Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T21:42:49Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"﻿Parent Algora bounty: #743\n\n## Bug\n\n`apps/api/src/controllers/authController.js` parses register and login request bodies with `registerSchema.parse(req.body)` and `loginSchema.parse(req.body)` directly. When either body is invalid, Zod throws a `ZodError` before the controller can return the API JSON error envelope.\n\nThis issue is limited only to the creator of this issue. This means that only the issue author can attempt to solve this issue. If you would like to work on it, please create another issue with the same contents and refer to issue #743 for more information.\n\n## Steps to reproduce\n\nCall `POST /api/auth/register` or `POST /api/auth/login` with a body such as:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"email\": \"not-an-email\",\n  \"password\": \"short\"\n}\n```\n\n## Expected behavior\n\nThe auth endpoint should return:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"success\": false,\n  \"message\": \"Invalid request body\"\n}\n```\n\nwith status `400`.\n\n## Actual behavior\n\nThe controller throws a `ZodError` instead of returning the predictable API error response.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\nCatch `ZodError` around auth schema parsing and route it through the existing `fail` response helper with status `400` for both register and login.\n\n## Validation plan\n\n- Add focused regression coverage for invalid register and login request bodies.\n- Confirm the endpoints return the existing `{ success: false, message }` JSON shape with HTTP 400.\n- Run `node --test apps/api/src/tests/authValidation.test.js apps/api/src/tests/health.test.js`.\n\n## Safety\n\nNo payout, contact, credential, wallet, or off-platform payment details should be posted publicly.\r\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/10966/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/10966/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ethereum/ethereum-org-website/issues/18433","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ethereum/ethereum-org-website","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ethereum/ethereum-org-website/issues/18433/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ethereum/ethereum-org-website/issues/18433/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ethereum/ethereum-org-website/issues/18433/events","html_url":"https://github.com/ethereum/ethereum-org-website/issues/18433","id":4699525714,"node_id":"I_kwDOBvEA_s8AAAABGB0SUg","number":18433,"title":"Suggest a staking product or service","user":{"login":"luganodes-visvesh","id":294104015,"node_id":"U_kgDOEYerzw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/294104015?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/luganodes-visvesh","html_url":"https://github.com/luganodes-visvesh","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luganodes-visvesh/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luganodes-visvesh/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luganodes-visvesh/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luganodes-visvesh/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luganodes-visvesh/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luganodes-visvesh/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luganodes-visvesh/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luganodes-visvesh/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/luganodes-visvesh/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":6799206342,"node_id":"LA_kwDOBvEA_s8AAAABlUOnxg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ethereum/ethereum-org-website/labels/product%20%F0%9F%A7%B0","name":"product 🧰","color":"fef2c0","default":false,"description":"This involves a product listing"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-06-19T09:22:06Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T21:14:16Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Project name\n\nLuganodes\n\n### Product type\n\nStaking as a service\n\n### If other product type, please describe\n\nInstitutional-Grade, also an RPC provider\n\n### Logo\n\n<img width=\"1209\" height=\"678\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/b23e57e3-ae89-47e2-8b74-9bf6d03fa861\" />\n\n### Description\n\nLuganodes is a world-class, non-custodial blockchain infrastructure provider, securing $2B+ in staked assets, tailored for institutions. Operating across 40+ PoS networks, 50+ institutional clients, Luganodes maintains 99.9% uptime, with an emphasis on security and compliance.\n\n### Website\n\nwww.luganodes.com\n\n### If software is involved, is everything open source?\n\nPortions of code are open source: provide link(s) to project repo(s)\n\n### Is the project a fork? If yes, which project was forked?\n\nNo\n\n### Is the product out of beta development?\n\nYes product is out of beta development and we have live customers as well\nWe have a batch contract \nWe have built open source tool for batch consolidation\nhttps://github.com/Luganodes/Pectra-Batch-Contract\nhttps://github.com/Luganodes/pectra-cli\nthe batch deposit contract is forked\nExit functionality on Api utilises a striped down version of the staking deposit cli\n\n### What wallets support the product or service?\n\nIntegrated with WalletConnect so support the 520+ wallets connected with WalletConnect\n\n### If the product or service enables staking with <32 ETH, what is the minimum ETH required to stake?\n\nNative staking does not allow below 32 ETH (Min 32)\nPooled staking offering allows below 32 ETH\nETH pooled staking enabled via stakewise no minimum ETH requirements \nNo staking requirements as such\n\n### If a service, what are the fees associated with using the service?\n\nmonthly commission on earning\nbased on tiered approach on the amount being staked (varies from client to client)\nInflationary rewards from staking\n\n\n### If the product or service involved a liquidity token, what are the tokens involved?\n\nno liquidity token involved\n\n### What date did the project or service go live?\n\nHave been live since Q4 2022 Ethereum staking services started Q3 2023 https://explorer.rated.network/o/Luganodes\n\n### Has the project undergone an external security audit?\n\nNo \nWe are undergoing Audit from Quantstamp\n\n\n### Has the project undergone any security bug bounties?\n\nNo\n\n### Is the project being actively maintained?\n\nYes\n\n### Is the product or service free of trusted/human intermediaries?\n\nNo we perform KYC for institutional clients\nWe do not have keys that needed to be trusted with humans\nBut after Pectra the private key of the withdrawal address is managed by the client always and we do not have access to it\nWithdrawal address is managed by the client always so we do not have access to it\n\n\n### If a pooled staking service, can users participate as a node operator without permission?\n\nWe have a pooled staking service offering\nUsers cannot operate as a node operator even if applying for pooled staking\nStaking to the already existing node is permissionless\n\n\n### If listing a staking-as-a-service, are users required to sign-up for an account?\n\nYes account needed for dApp\nAccount needed for API(and API key)\ndApp requires Wallet login and normal login\n\n\n### If listing as staking-as-a-service, who has access to the signing keys?\n\nWe solely have custody of the validator signing keys, Withdrawal address access remains with user/clients only.\n\n### If a pooled staking service or SaaS provider, what type of withdrawal credentials are being utilized / who holds the withdrawal keys?\n\nIn cases of SaaS we use both(0x01 and 0x02) depending on user request (chosen by the user)\nWe hold the keystore and mnemonic and client holds the withdrawal address\nIn case of pooled staking it’s a smart contract (using Stakewise vaults)\nWithdrawal account chosen by the user\n\n### If a pooled staking service or SaaS provider, what percent of node operators are running a super-majority client?\n\n100% on CL AND equal share on EL(Validator can choose any EL client)\nOn Consensus no diversity only Lighthouse on EL we use Reth Nethermind Geth\nNo Super majority\n\n\n### If listing node or client tooling, which consensus layer clients (Lighthouse, Teku, Nimbus, or Prysm) are supported?\n\nLighthouse is supported \nthere are no other options to switch\n\n### What platforms are supported?\n\nWebsite GUI\n\n### What user interfaces are supported?\n\nBrowser app we have REST APIs and Website GUI\n\n### Social media links\n\nTwitter/X: https://x.com/luganodes\nLinkedIn: https://www.linkedin.com/company/luganodes\nYoutube: https://www.youtube.com/@luganodes\n\n### Would you like to work on this issue?\n\n- [ ] Yes\n- [ ] No","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ethereum/ethereum-org-website/issues/18433/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ethereum/ethereum-org-website/issues/18433/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ethereum/ethereum-org-website/issues/18211","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ethereum/ethereum-org-website","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ethereum/ethereum-org-website/issues/18211/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ethereum/ethereum-org-website/issues/18211/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ethereum/ethereum-org-website/issues/18211/events","html_url":"https://github.com/ethereum/ethereum-org-website/issues/18211","id":4465057466,"node_id":"I_kwDOBvEA_s8AAAABCiNeug","number":18211,"title":"Suggest a wallet: Cloaked","user":{"login":"blmalone","id":15608778,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE1NjA4Nzc4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/15608778?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/blmalone","html_url":"https://github.com/blmalone","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blmalone/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blmalone/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blmalone/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blmalone/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blmalone/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blmalone/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blmalone/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blmalone/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/blmalone/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":6799206342,"node_id":"LA_kwDOBvEA_s8AAAABlUOnxg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ethereum/ethereum-org-website/labels/product%20%F0%9F%A7%B0","name":"product 🧰","color":"fef2c0","default":false,"description":"This involves a product listing"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[{"login":"konopkja","id":100724231,"node_id":"U_kgDOBgDuBw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/100724231?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konopkja","html_url":"https://github.com/konopkja","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konopkja/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konopkja/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konopkja/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konopkja/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konopkja/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konopkja/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konopkja/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konopkja/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konopkja/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":3,"created_at":"2026-05-17T21:56:38Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T21:13:43Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":{"login":"konopkja","id":100724231,"node_id":"U_kgDOBgDuBw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/100724231?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konopkja","html_url":"https://github.com/konopkja","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konopkja/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konopkja/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konopkja/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konopkja/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konopkja/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konopkja/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konopkja/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konopkja/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konopkja/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"## Project info\n\n### Wallet name\n\nCloaked\n\n### What type of wallet?\n\nEOA with Smart Features (EIP-7702)\n\n### Wallet description\n\nCloaked is a self-custodial Ethereum wallet with built-in privacy features. It uses stealth addresses, ENS-based receive names, EIP-7702 account upgrades, and privacy pools so users can send, receive, swap, bridge, and cash out without reusing a single public address for all activity.\n\n### Wallet logo\n\nTransparent PNG: https://drive.google.com/file/d/1GDWcVntd27Yx8AXUgd63qbBb7JY9oPUH/view?usp=sharing\n\n\n### Background color for brand logo\n\n#7B4DFF\n\n### URL to the project\n\nApplication: https://app.clkd.xyz\nLanding Page: https://clkd.xyz\nDocs: https://clkd.xyz/docs\n\n### When did the wallet go live to users?\n\nProduction web app release: March, 2026.\n\nThe project is built by a team with prior wallet/blockchain experience at Optimism, ConsenSys, Gemini, and Bastion, as noted on the Cloaked website.\n\n### What are the fees users may be paying for using your wallet product?\n\n- Sends: users pay network/gas fees. No separate Cloaked service fee is charged on sends, though network fee estimates include an operational buffer and all fees are disclosed before execution.\n- Swaps and bridges: network fees plus a Cloaked service fee currently documented as 0.85% of the input amount.\n- Privacy pool deposits/withdrawals: network fees and applicable pool/protocol/Cloaked fees are disclosed before execution.\n- Off-ramp: network fees, route costs, third-party fees, and Cloaked service fees may apply and are disclosed before execution.\n\nDocs:\n\n- https://clkd.xyz/docs/using-cloaked\n- https://clkd.xyz/docs/swaps\n- https://clkd.xyz/docs/privacy-pools\n- https://clkd.xyz/docs/off-ramp\n- https://clkd.xyz/docs/terms\n\n### Does the wallet have an active development team?\n\nYes. Cloaked is actively developed by Cloaked Technologies, Inc. Public source-available components include:\n\n- https://github.com/cloakedxyz/clkd-stealth\n- https://github.com/cloakedxyz/clkd-recovery\n- https://github.com/cloakedxyz/clkd-privacy-pools\n- https://github.com/cloakedxyz/clkd-peer\n\n### Is the wallet globally accessible?\n\nThe wallet is available as a web app. Cloaked does not require wallet-account KYC for ordinary wallet use. Users must comply with the Terms of Service, including sanctions restrictions. Off-ramp availability depends on third-party providers, payment methods, liquidity, buyer activity, supported jurisdictions, and applicable laws.\n\nDocs:\n\n- https://clkd.xyz/docs/terms\n- https://clkd.xyz/docs/privacy\n- https://clkd.xyz/docs/off-ramp\n\n### Is the wallet available in multiple languages?\n\nEnglish. (more coming soon)\n\n### What social links are there for the project?\n\n- Website: https://clkd.xyz\n- Docs: https://clkd.xyz/docs\n- GitHub: https://github.com/cloakedxyz\n- X/Twitter: https://x.com/staycloakedxyz\n- Farcaster: https://farcaster.xyz/cloaked\n\n## Device\n\n### Does the wallet have a mobile app? If yes, which operating systems are supported (iOS, Android)?\n\nCloaked is publicly available as a web app and as a Farcaster mini app. A native mobile app is being worked on.\n\n### Does the wallet have a desktop app? If yes, which operating systems are supported (Windows, Mac, Linux)?\n\nNo native desktop app. The wallet is available through the browser at https://app.clkd.xyz.\n\n### Does the wallet have a browser extension? If yes, which browsers are supported (Chromium, Firefox, Safari)?\n\nBrowser extension coming soon.\n\n### Is it a hardware wallet?\n\nNo. Cloaked is not a hardware wallet. Users can register/sign with an external wallet, including hardware-backed wallet providers where supported by that wallet, but Cloaked itself is software.\n\n## Security\n\n### What is the availability of your source code?\n\nSource available.\n\nCore recovery and cryptographic SDK components are public under the Cloaked GitHub organization. The full hosted app/server codebase is not fully open source at this time.\n\nPublic components:\n\n- https://github.com/cloakedxyz/clkd-stealth\n- https://github.com/cloakedxyz/clkd-recovery\n- https://github.com/cloakedxyz/clkd-privacy-pools\n- https://github.com/cloakedxyz/clkd-peer\n\n### What license is the wallet software released under?\n\nPublic SDK/recovery components are MIT licensed. Proprietary hosted application/server components are not fully open source.\n\n### Who holds the private keys?\n\nUsers hold the spending capability. Cloaked is self-custodial and does not custody funds or private keys. The spending capability remains client-side and is required to authorize transactions. Cloaked coordinates address derivation, balance tracking, transaction construction, and relay submission, but cannot move funds independently.\n\nDocs:\n\n- https://clkd.xyz/docs\n- https://clkd.xyz/docs/how-it-works\n- https://clkd.xyz/docs/recovery\n- https://clkd.xyz/docs/faq\n- https://clkd.xyz/docs/terms\n\n### Please describe the measures taken to ensure the wallet's security and provide documentation wherever possible\n\n- Self-custodial key model: the spending capability never leaves the user's device.\n- Separate viewing and spending capabilities: Cloaked receives scoped viewing material for address detection and balance tracking, while spending authority remains client-side.\n- Passkey/WebAuthn PRF support for phishing-resistant authentication where supported by the device/browser.\n- Wallet + PIN mode requires a user-entered PIN combined with wallet signatures, adding friction against blind-signing flows.\n- Encrypted backup/recovery flow: passkey users can export a password-encrypted backup file, and recovery runs through the public recovery app.\n- EIP-7702 / Porto-based execution requires explicit user authorization for account upgrades and payments.\n- Transaction quotes disclose expected fees before confirmation.\n\nDocs:\n\n- https://clkd.xyz/docs/how-it-works\n- https://clkd.xyz/docs/passkey-safety\n- https://clkd.xyz/docs/recovery\n- https://clkd.xyz/docs/faq\n- https://github.com/cloakedxyz/clkd-stealth\n- https://github.com/cloakedxyz/clkd-recovery\n\n### Has the wallet's smart contract code or security modules been audited?\n\nCloaked uses Paradigm's EIP-7702 smart account infrastructure through Porto. Paradigm's 7702 smart accounts were audited by Riley H, Kaden, and Milotruck, and Paradigm maintains a live bug bounty: https://porto.sh/contracts/security-and-bug-bounty\n\n### Does the wallet have an internal security team?\n\nYes, security is handled by the active Cloaked development team. Public docs describe the self-custodial model, passkey safety, recovery, privacy pool trust model, and non-custodial transaction relay model.\n\n### Any other security testing that should be noted?\n\nThe project has automated tests across SDK, server, app, chain indexing, and shared UI packages. Public source-available packages expose the cryptographic/recovery logic for review. Security-sensitive public documentation is available at:\n\n- https://clkd.xyz/docs/how-it-works\n- https://clkd.xyz/docs/passkey-safety\n- https://clkd.xyz/docs/recovery\n- https://clkd.xyz/docs/privacy-pools\n- https://clkd.xyz/docs/terms\n\n### Scam protection?\n\nCloaked uses explicit passkey or wallet-signature authorization for sensitive actions, shows quotes/fees before confirmation, and wallet+PIN mode adds an intentional confirmation step to reduce accidental or blind signing. Cloaked does not currently advertise a general malicious-token or malicious-contract detection engine.\n\n## Features\n\n### Does the wallet support connecting to Ethereum applications?\n\nPartially. Cloaked is primarily a wallet web app today. A Chromium browser extension for EIP-6963 dapp provider injection is in development, but there is no public extension store link yet.\n\n### Does the wallet support connecting to a hardware wallet?\n\nYes, indirectly. Users can authenticate with external wallet providers, including hardware-backed wallets where supported by that provider. Cloaked does not provide a native USB/Bluetooth hardware-wallet integration.\n\nDocs: https://clkd.xyz/docs/developers\n\n### Does the wallet support importing Ethereum RPC endpoints?\n\nNo public custom-RPC import feature is documented today. Cloaked currently supports the networks configured by the service.\n\n### Does the wallet support viewing and interacting with NFTs?\n\nNo general NFT gallery/support is documented. Cloaked has Cloakie NFT-related functionality internally, but general NFT viewing/interaction should be treated as not supported for the ethereum.org listing.\n\n### Does the wallet support staking directly?\n\nNo direct ETH staking support is documented.\n\n### Does the wallet support swaps directly?\n\nYes. Cloaked supports direct swaps, powered by Uniswap routing.\n\nDocs: https://clkd.xyz/docs/swaps\n\n### Does the wallet support bridging directly?\n\nYes. Cloaked supports cross-chain bridging/routing, including ETH on Ethereum to ETH on Base, powered by Uniswap/Across routes.\n\nDocs: https://clkd.xyz/docs/swaps\n\n### Does the wallet support multi-chain networks?\n\nYes. Cloaked currently supports Ethereum and Base.\n\nDocs: https://clkd.xyz/docs\n\n### Which Ethereum Layer 2 networks does the wallet support?\n\nBase.\n\nDocs: https://clkd.xyz/docs\n\n### Does the wallet allow the user to customize gas fees?\n\nNo manual custom gas fee UI is documented. Cloaked estimates and displays transaction/network fees before confirmation, and relays authorized transactions on the user's behalf.\n\nDocs:\n\n- https://clkd.xyz/docs/using-cloaked\n- https://clkd.xyz/docs/terms\n\n### Does the wallet support sending transactions to ENS addresses?\n\nYes. Cloaked is ENS-native for receiving through `username.clkd.eth`, supports direct payment pages via `username.clkd.id`, and its API supports destinations as `0x...` addresses or ENS names.\n\nDocs:\n\n- https://clkd.xyz/docs\n- https://clkd.xyz/docs/using-cloaked\n- https://clkd.xyz/docs/api-reference\n\n### Does the wallet support importing or automatically querying and displaying ERC-20 tokens?\n\nYes. Cloaked supports ERC-20 token balances on supported chains using the Uniswap default token list plus native ETH. The app/API support token catalogs, token lookup, balances, sends, swaps, and bridges for supported tokens.\n\nDocs:\n\n- https://clkd.xyz/docs\n- https://clkd.xyz/docs/api-reference\n\n### Does the wallet support EIP-1559 (type 2) transactions?\n\nYes. Cloaked supports EIP-1559 fee handling for Ethereum Mainnet transactions submitted through its relay flow.\n\n### Does the wallet have any recovery options?\n\nYes. Passkey users can create a password-encrypted backup file and recover through https://recovery.clkd.xyz. Wallet + PIN users recover through their wallet seed/private key plus their PIN. Cloaked does not custody keys and cannot reset lost passkeys/PINs.\n\nDocs: https://clkd.xyz/docs/recovery\n\n## Finance\n\n### Does the wallet have fiat on-ramps through credit/debit cards, wire transfers, or bank transfers (ACH)?\n\nNo fiat on-ramp is documented.\n\n### Does the wallet support withdrawals to fiat?\n\nYes. Cloaked integrates Peer for peer-to-peer off-ramp/cash-out flows. Availability depends on Peer, buyer liquidity, payment method, supported jurisdictions, and applicable laws.\n\nDocs:\n\n- https://clkd.xyz/docs/off-ramp\n- https://clkd.xyz/docs/terms\n\n## Smart contract\n\n### Is the wallet a multi-signature wallet?\n\nNo.\n\n### Does the wallet support social recovery?\n\nNo guardian/social recovery support is documented.\n\n### Does the wallet support bundled transactions?\n\nYes. Cloaked uses EIP-7702/Porto smart account execution and can combine multiple stealth-address inputs and route sends/swaps/bridges/off-ramp actions through bundled transaction flows.\n\nDocs:\n\n- https://clkd.xyz/docs/how-it-works\n- https://clkd.xyz/docs/swaps\n- https://clkd.xyz/docs/off-ramp\n\n### Does the wallet support Smart Accounts (EIP-4337)?\n\nNo.\n\n### Does the wallet support Account Upgrades (EIP-7702)?\n\nYes.\n\nDocs: https://clkd.xyz/docs/how-it-works\n\n## Support\n\n### Who can the ethereum.org team can contact regarding the wallet in future?\n\nsupport@clkd.xyz\n\nX/Twitter: https://x.com/staycloakedxyz\n\n### Does the wallet have a dedicated support team?\n\nUsers should contact support@clkd.xyz or join the Cloaked Telegram support channel at https://t.me/+pXdSklUm5bsxMmMx. The public docs also direct users to support@clkd.xyz for help with passkey concerns.\n\nDocs: https://clkd.xyz/docs/passkey-safety\n\n### What educational resources/documentation do you provide to users?\n\n- User docs: https://clkd.xyz/docs\n- How it works: https://clkd.xyz/docs/how-it-works\n- Using Cloaked: https://clkd.xyz/docs/using-cloaked\n- Swaps & bridging: https://clkd.xyz/docs/swaps\n- Privacy pools: https://clkd.xyz/docs/privacy-pools\n- Passkey safety: https://clkd.xyz/docs/passkey-safety\n- Account recovery: https://clkd.xyz/docs/recovery\n- FAQ: https://clkd.xyz/docs/faq\n- Developers: https://clkd.xyz/docs/developers\n- API reference: https://clkd.xyz/docs/api-reference\n\n## Extra\n\n### Does the wallet have any integrated tools not mentioned above?\n\nCloaked includes privacy-specific wallet features:\n\n- Stealth addresses for per-payment receive addresses.\n- ENS-native receive names through `username.clkd.eth`.\n- `username.clkd.id` payment pages.\n- Incognito balances through Privacy Pools.\n- Client-side recovery tooling.\n- Developer API and SDK access for stealth-address payment integrations.\n\n### Would you like to work on this issue?\n\nYes.\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ethereum/ethereum-org-website/issues/18211/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ethereum/ethereum-org-website/issues/18211/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ethereum/ethereum-org-website/issues/16404","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ethereum/ethereum-org-website","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ethereum/ethereum-org-website/issues/16404/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ethereum/ethereum-org-website/issues/16404/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ethereum/ethereum-org-website/issues/16404/events","html_url":"https://github.com/ethereum/ethereum-org-website/issues/16404","id":3471622330,"node_id":"I_kwDOBvEA_s7O7MC6","number":16404,"title":"Suggest a wallet: Ownbit","user":{"login":"jtomtan","id":11899268,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExODk5MjY4","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11899268?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/jtomtan","html_url":"https://github.com/jtomtan","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jtomtan/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jtomtan/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jtomtan/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jtomtan/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jtomtan/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jtomtan/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jtomtan/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jtomtan/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jtomtan/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":3982036190,"node_id":"LA_kwDOBvEA_s7tWQze","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ethereum/ethereum-org-website/labels/wallet%20%F0%9F%91%9B","name":"wallet 👛","color":"0983DF","default":false,"description":"This issue relates to adding or changing a wallet"},{"id":6799206342,"node_id":"LA_kwDOBvEA_s8AAAABlUOnxg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ethereum/ethereum-org-website/labels/product%20%F0%9F%A7%B0","name":"product 🧰","color":"fef2c0","default":false,"description":"This involves a product listing"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[{"login":"konopkja","id":100724231,"node_id":"U_kgDOBgDuBw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/100724231?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konopkja","html_url":"https://github.com/konopkja","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konopkja/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konopkja/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konopkja/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konopkja/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konopkja/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konopkja/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konopkja/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konopkja/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konopkja/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}],"milestone":null,"comments":9,"created_at":"2025-10-01T01:18:37Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T21:13:42Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":{"login":"konopkja","id":100724231,"node_id":"U_kgDOBgDuBw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/100724231?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/konopkja","html_url":"https://github.com/konopkja","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konopkja/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konopkja/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konopkja/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konopkja/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konopkja/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konopkja/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konopkja/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konopkja/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/konopkja/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Wallet name\n\nOwnbit\n\n### What type of wallet?\n\nEOA\n\n### Wallet description\n\nOwnbit is a non-custodial mobile wallet that supports Ethereum and other EVM networks, with a long-standing focus on multisignature features. It has been widely used by teams and individuals in the Ethereum ecosystem for secure multisig management.\n\n### Wallet logo\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a96dc6a1-534c-4bca-a6de-c46c73e44b51)\n\n### Background color for brand logo\n\n#FFFFFF\n\n### URL to the project\n\nhttps://ownbit.io/\n\n### When did the wallet go live to users?\n\nYear 2018\n\n### What are the fees users may be paying for using your wallet product?\n\nBasic usage (standard personal wallets) is completely free. Advanced features such as cold wallet and multisig require a subscription (Ownbit Premium), with annual membership tiers (Lv1–Lv3) instead of per-transaction fees.\n\n### Does the wallet have an active development team?\n\nYes. Github: https://github.com/bitbill\n\n### Is the wallet globally accessible?\n\nYes, globally accessible and no KYC needed currently.\n\n### Is the wallet available in multiple languages?\n\nEnglish / Simplified Chinese / Traditional Chinese / Japanese / Korean / Russian / Spanish / German / French / Portuguese / Italian / Indonesian / Turkish / Thai / Vietnamese / Filipino\n\n### What social links are there for the project?\n\nTwitter：https://twitter.com/OwnbitWallet\n\n### Does the wallet have a mobile app? If yes, which operating systems are supported (iOS, Android)?\n\niOS: https://apps.apple.com/app/id1321798216\nAndroid: https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.bitbill.www\n\n### Does the wallet have a desktop app? If yes, which operating systems are supported (Windows, Mac, Linux)?\n\nNo.\n\n### Does the wallet have a browser extension? If yes, which browsers are supported (Chromium, Firefox, Safari)?\n\nNo.\n\n### Is it a hardware wallet?\n\nNo, Ownbit is not a traditional hardware wallet. It provides cold wallet functionality by using two mobile devices: one kept fully offline and one online. Transactions are signed on the offline device and broadcast by the online device via QR code scanning, offering security comparable to hardware wallets.\n\n### What is the availability of your source code?\n\nClosed source\n\n### What license is the wallet software released under?\n\nMIT\n\n### Who holds the private keys?\n\nUsers hold their private keys entirely, and back them up via a mnemonic phrase. Addresses are generated according to BIP39 and BIP44 standards, so funds remain accessible even without the app. For Ethereum multisig, Ownbit uses open-sourced smart contracts published on Etherscan.\n\n### Please describe the measures taken to ensure the wallet's security and provide documentation wherever possible\n\nMultisig security: Ownbit’s Ethereum multisig contracts are open-sourced at [GitHub](https://github.com/bitbill/ownbit-multisig-contracts)\n. They have been in continuous production use for over 5 years, securing tens of millions of USD in assets. While they have not undergone a formal third-party audit, the contracts are publicly available, reviewed by external developers, and even reused by other projects.\n\nCold wallet security: Ownbit offers a mobile-based cold wallet mode using two devices (one kept permanently offline). This design ensures private keys never touch the internet. We have published detailed documentation explaining and demonstrating its security model: [Ownbit Cold Wallet Security](https://bitbill.oss-accelerate.aliyuncs.com/h5/app/ownbit_cold_wallet_is_more_secure_than_hardware_cold_wallet_en.html)\n.\n\nBug bounty / external review: While we do not yet run a formal bug bounty, we encourage public review of our open-source contracts and security documentation, and welcome responsible disclosure.\n\n### Has the wallet's smart contract code or security modules been audited?\n\nNot formally audited by a third-party company, but the multisig contracts are open source and have been referenced and used by multiple teams and users. GitHub: ownbit-multisig-contracts .\n\n### Does the wallet have an internal security team?\n\nWe do not have a dedicated internal security team. However, Ownbit is built and maintained by a small, highly experienced group of developers who have been building Bitcoin and Ethereum wallets since 2013.\n\n### Any other security testing that should be noted?\n\nOur approach emphasizes transparency and user-verifiable security. We encourage users with technical backgrounds to review and validate our design, particularly the cold wallet mode where private keys never touch the internet. Documentation: [Cold Wallet Security](https://bitbill.oss-accelerate.aliyuncs.com/h5/app/ownbit_cold_wallet_is_more_secure_than_hardware_cold_wallet_en.html)\n.\n\n### Scam protection?\n\nYes. Ownbit focuses on user safety. When interacting with DApps, the wallet implements logic to warn users about potential risks and performs basic checks to help protect against common scams. For example, Ownbit includes filters to block known phishing addresses and provides alerts to help users avoid interacting with malicious contracts.\n\n### Does the wallet support connecting to Ethereum applications?\n\nes. Ownbit supports WalletConnect for connecting to Ethereum applications.\n\n### Does the wallet support connecting to a hardware wallet?\n\nNo\n\n### Does the wallet support importing Ethereum RPC endpoints?\n\nNo\n\n### Does the wallet support viewing and interacting with NFTs?\n\nYes\n\n### Does the wallet support staking directly?\n\nNo\n\n### Does the wallet support swaps directly?\n\nNo\n\n### Does the wallet support bridging directly?\n\nNo\n\n### Does the wallet support multi-chain networks?\n\nYes. Multi-chain support is built-in. Ownbit supports Ethereum Layer 2 networks such as Arbitrum, Optimism, and Base, as well as popular EVM-compatible chains including BNB Smart Chain and Polygon.\n\n### Which Ethereum Layer 2 networks does the wallet support?\n\nOptimism, Arbitrum, BASE\n\n### Does the wallet allow the user to customize gas fees?\n\nYes. During the send process, users can open advanced options to customize gas fees, gas limit, and add custom HEX data.\n\n### Does the wallet support sending transactions to ENS addresses?\n\nYes. ENS is supported.\n\n### Does the wallet support importing or automatically querying and displaying ERC-20 tokens?\n\nYes. Users can search and add ERC-20 tokens by symbol, name, or contract address.\n\n### Does the wallet support EIP-1559 (type 2) transactions?\n\nYes, type 2 transactions by default. \n\n### Does the wallet have any recovery options?\n\nYes. Users can self-recover all assets by importing their mnemonic phrase into any BIP39-compatible wallet (e.g. Trust Wallet, imToken).\nFor multisig assets, since the contracts are open source, users can simulate and call the smart contract directly to transfer assets. Detailed recovery instructions are also available in the app (Homepage → top-left Help → “How to self-recover MultiSig assets”).\n\n### Does the wallet have fiat on-ramps through credit/debit cards, wire transfers, or bank transfers (ACH)?\n\nNo\n\n### Does the wallet support withdrawals to fiat?\n\nNo\n\n### Is the wallet a multi-signature wallet?\n\nYes\n\n### Does the wallet support social recovery?\n\nNo\n\n### Does the wallet support bundled transactions?\n\nNo\n\n### Who can the ethereum.org team can contact regarding the wallet in future?\n\nYou can contact Ownbit team through the following ways:\n\nEmail: [support@ownbit.io](mailto:support@ownbit.io)\nTelegram: https://t.me/ownbit\nTwitter: https://twitter.com/OwnbitWallet\n\n### Does the wallet have a dedicated support team?\n\nYes. Ownbit provides 24/7 support via email ([support@ownbit.io](mailto:support@ownbit.io)) and Telegram (https://t.me/ownbit), with response times often within minutes.\n\n### What educational resources/documentation do you provide to users?\n\nHelp documentation is built into the app and can be accessed from the homepage (top-left Help icon).\n\n### Does the wallet have any integrated tools not mentioned above?\n\nYes. In addition to multisig and inheritance, Ownbit also provides built-in Bitcoin/Ethereum signing tools, as well as an Ethereum multisig self-recovery tool. These allow users to conveniently sign transactions or recover multisig assets even in the event Ownbit is unavailable.\n\n### Would you like to work on this issue?\n\n- [x] Yes\n- [ ] No","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ethereum/ethereum-org-website/issues/16404/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/ethereum/ethereum-org-website/issues/16404/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":"reopened","pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dev-kp-eloper/BountyScout/issues/398","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dev-kp-eloper/BountyScout","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dev-kp-eloper/BountyScout/issues/398/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dev-kp-eloper/BountyScout/issues/398/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/dev-kp-eloper/BountyScout/issues/398/events","html_url":"https://github.com/dev-kp-eloper/BountyScout/issues/398","id":4823037843,"node_id":"I_kwDOSmCMss8AAAABH3m3kw","number":398,"title":"🎯 Bounty Alert: 10 New Opportunityies found","user":{"login":"github-actions[bot]","id":41898282,"node_id":"MDM6Qm90NDE4OTgyODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/15368?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/github-actions","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/github-actions%5Bbot%5D