d-only)](https://github.com/mswell/bountybrain/issues/1)\n- **Repository:** [mswell/bountybrain](https://github.com/mswell/bountybrain)\n- **Comments:** 1\n- **Last Updated:** 2026-07-06T13:38:44Z\n\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vansh-09/BountyScout/issues/282/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vansh-09/BountyScout/issues/282/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/10962","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/10962/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/10962/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/10962/events","html_url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/10962","id":4820029282,"node_id":"I_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABH0vPYg","number":10962,"title":"Async route rejections should reach the global error handler","user":{"login":"ewbd09-svg","id":265281923,"node_id":"U_kgDOD8_hgw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/265281923?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ewbd09-svg","html_url":"https://github.com/ewbd09-svg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ewbd09-svg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ewbd09-svg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ewbd09-svg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ewbd09-svg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ewbd09-svg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ewbd09-svg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ewbd09-svg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ewbd09-svg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ewbd09-svg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-07-06T14:20:37Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T14:20:37Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Parent bounty: #743\n\n## Bug\n\nThe API runs on Express 4 and mounts async controller functions directly in its routers. Express 4 does not automatically forward rejected promises from async route handlers to the global error middleware.\n\nFor example, `postJob()` calls `createJobSchema.parse(req.body)` inside an async controller. If validation throws, the async function returns a rejected promise, but the route is mounted as `jobRoutes.post(\"/\", postJob)` with no `.catch(next)` wrapper. That can bypass `errorHandler`, causing an unhandled route rejection or an unresolved request instead of the shared error response path.\n\n## Expected behavior\n\nAsync route handlers should consistently forward thrown errors and rejected promises to Express via `next`, so the existing global `errorHandler` remains the single error-response path.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Add a small async route wrapper that resolves a controller result and forwards rejections to `next`.\n- Apply it to the existing async controller route mounts.\n- Add focused regression coverage showing an async validation rejection reaches the global error handler.\n- Do not change the validation response contract or implement Zod-specific 400 handling in this issue.\n\nThis issue is limited only to the creator of this issue. This means that only the issue author can attempt to solve this issue. If you would like to work on it, please create another issue with the same contents and refer to issue #743 for more information.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/10962/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/10962/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/10960","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/10960/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/10960/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/10960/events","html_url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/10960","id":4819998720,"node_id":"I_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABH0tYAA","number":10960,"title":"Card component should forward native section props","user":{"login":"cnbright","id":31305864,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMxMzA1ODY0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/31305864?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/cnbright","html_url":"https://github.com/cnbright","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cnbright/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cnbright/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cnbright/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cnbright/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cnbright/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cnbright/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cnbright/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cnbright/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/cnbright/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-07-06T14:16:51Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T14:16:51Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Parent Algora bounty: #743\n\n## Bug\n\nThe shared `Card` component in `packages/ui/src/Card.tsx` renders a `<section>` but only accepts `title` and `children`. Callers cannot pass normal section attributes such as `className`, `id`, `aria-*`, `data-*`, or custom `style`, which makes the shared component hard to use in accessible and styled app pages without wrapping it in extra DOM.\n\n## Expected behavior\n\n- `Card` should accept native section props via `React.HTMLAttributes<HTMLElement>`.\n- Existing title and children rendering should remain unchanged.\n- Default border/radius/padding styling should be preserved.\n- Caller-provided `style` should be able to extend or override the defaults.\n- The fix should stay limited to `packages/ui/src/Card.tsx`.\n\n## Validation plan\n\n- Run a focused TypeScript compile command for `packages/ui/src/Card.tsx`.\n- Run `git diff --check`.\n\nThis issue is limited only to the creator of this issue. This means that only the issue author can attempt to solve this issue. If you would like to work on it, please create another issue with the same contents and refer to issue #743 for more information.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/10960/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/10960/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/10958","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/10958/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/10958/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/10958/events","html_url":"https://github.com/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/10958","id":4819964195,"node_id":"I_kwDOSfPzA88AAAABH0rRIw","number":10958,"title":"List services should not expose mutable backing arrays","user":{"login":"ewbd09-svg","id":265281923,"node_id":"U_kgDOD8_hgw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/265281923?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ewbd09-svg","html_url":"https://github.com/ewbd09-svg","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ewbd09-svg/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ewbd09-svg/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ewbd09-svg/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ewbd09-svg/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ewbd09-svg/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ewbd09-svg/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ewbd09-svg/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ewbd09-svg/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ewbd09-svg/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-07-06T14:13:29Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T14:13:29Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"Parent bounty: #743\n\n## Bug\n\nThe API list service functions return their in-memory backing arrays directly. Consumers that receive a list can mutate the service state by pushing records into the returned array or editing a returned record object.\n\nAffected functions:\n\n- `listUsers()`\n- `listJobs()`\n- `listProposals()`\n- `listReviews()`\n- `listMessages()`\n- `listNotifications()`\n\n## Expected behavior\n\nList functions should return defensive copies so callers can read records without mutating the backing store outside the service create functions.\n\n## Scope\n\nKeep the fix limited to returning cloned list records from the list service functions, plus focused service-level regression coverage showing returned arrays and records cannot mutate internal state.\n\nThis issue is limited only to the creator of this issue. This means that only the issue author can attempt to solve this issue. If you would like to work on it, please create another issue with the same contents and refer to issue #743 for more information.","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/10958/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/SecureBananaLabs/bug-bounty/issues/10958/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Saber5656/openintercom/issues/35","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Saber5656/openintercom","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Saber5656/openintercom/issues/35/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Saber5656/openintercom/issues/35/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Saber5656/openintercom/issues/35/events","html_url":"https://github.com/Saber5656/openintercom/issues/35","id":4819959865,"node_id":"I_kwDOTNkIZc8AAAABH0rAOQ","number":35,"title":"34: Security policy and disclosure docs","user":{"login":"Saber5656","id":177426695,"node_id":"U_kgDOCpNRBw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/177426695?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saber5656","html_url":"https://github.com/Saber5656","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saber5656/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saber5656/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saber5656/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saber5656/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saber5656/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saber5656/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saber5656/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saber5656/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Saber5656/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"labels":[{"id":11434530567,"node_id":"LA_kwDOTNkIZc8AAAACqY0XBw","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Saber5656/openintercom/labels/v1","name":"v1","color":"0e8a16","default":false,"description":"Required for the v1.0.0 release"},{"id":11434531034,"node_id":"LA_kwDOTNkIZc8AAAACqY0Y2g","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Saber5656/openintercom/labels/wave:5","name":"wave:5","color":"fef2c0","default":false,"description":"Verification & release wave"},{"id":11434531242,"node_id":"LA_kwDOTNkIZc8AAAACqY0Zqg","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Saber5656/openintercom/labels/area:security","name":"area:security","color":"e11d21","default":false,"description":"Security-relevant"},{"id":11434531613,"node_id":"LA_kwDOTNkIZc8AAAACqY0bHQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Saber5656/openintercom/labels/area:docs","name":"area:docs","color":"0075ca","default":false,"description":"Documentation"}],"state":"open","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":0,"created_at":"2026-07-06T14:12:59Z","updated_at":"2026-07-06T14:12:59Z","closed_at":null,"assignee":null,"author_association":"OWNER","active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"\n## Summary\n\nPublish the project's security posture: SECURITY.md (reporting, scope,\ncommitments), a public-facing threat-model digest, and a verification\nchecklist that the repo's scanning stack (from issue 02) is actually\narmed.\n\n## Context\n\nDESIGN §9 is the internal model; an OSS release needs the public contract:\nhow to report vulnerabilities, what's supported, what the product promises\n(§9.8) and refuses (ADR-005). GitHub repo settings themselves are\nowner-managed; this issue delivers docs + a verification checklist, not\nsettings changes.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `SECURITY.md`, `docs/security-model.md` (public digest)\n- Repo-scanning verification checklist (in the PR description / issue\n  comment, executed with the owner)\n\n## Detailed Requirements\n\n1. `SECURITY.md`:\n   - Reporting: GitHub Security Advisories (private) as the channel; no\n     email required v1; acknowledgment target ≤7 days, fix-or-plan\n     communicated ≤90 days; credit policy.\n   - Supported versions table (latest minor only during v1.x).\n   - **Deployment warnings, verbatim commitments**: never expose\n     `:8443`/`:8080` to the internet (ADR-005 wording); the CA-trust\n     model and what a leaked `data/` implies (CA key!); remote access =\n     your own VPN.\n   - Scope: what counts as a vulnerability here (auth bypass, CSP/CSRF\n     break, token leak, cert mis-issuance, media reaching the hub, DoS\n     below the §9.7 documented floor) vs. not (LAN flooding, physical\n     access to an unlocked station, user removing name constraints).\n   - Signing/checksums status (checksums now; cosign = roadmap).\n2. `docs/security-model.md`: 1–2 page digest of DESIGN §9 for users and\n   reviewers: diagram of trust boundaries (reuse §4 mermaid, simplified),\n   the five §9.8 commitments, residual-risk table (TOFU, user-CA,\n   LAN-DoS) in honest plain language, link to full DESIGN §9. This is the\n   page README's security section links to.\n3. Cross-file consistency: README (32) security summary, SECURITY.md and\n   security-model.md must not drift — single source rule: commitments\n   live word-for-word identical in SECURITY.md and are quoted elsewhere;\n   consistency asserted by a docs-lint grep script (extend\n   `scripts/docs-i18n-check.mjs` sibling `scripts/docs-consistency.mjs`).\n4. Scanning verification checklist (executed with repo owner; results\n   pasted into the issue):\n   `gh api repos/{o}/{r}` + web UI checks — CodeQL runs green on main;\n   Dependabot alerts + security updates enabled; secret scanning + push\n   protection enabled; private vulnerability reporting enabled; branch\n   protection/ruleset on main active. Any gap → owner action item\n   (agent does not change repo settings).\n5. Japanese note: SECURITY.md stays English (GitHub convention);\n   README.ja.md links it with one ja sentence of guidance (coordinate\n   with 33).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] SECURITY.md + security-model.md merged; linked from README and\n      from the admin UI Security panel caption (28 — text-only link\n      addition, coordinate if 28 already merged).\n- [ ] Commitments identical across files (consistency script green;\n      demonstrated failing on a scratch edit).\n- [ ] Private vulnerability reporting verified reachable (test advisory\n      draft created and discarded, or UI screenshot).\n- [ ] Scanning checklist fully executed; each item ✔ or an owner action\n      item filed.\n- [ ] Threat-model digest reviewed against DESIGN §9 for accuracy (no\n      overclaiming — especially around E2E encryption wording: DTLS-SRTP\n      peer-to-peer, hub relays SDP, hub compromise = active-MITM risk,\n      §9.1 wording reused).\n\n## Validation\n\nDocs-consistency script in CI; checklist evidence in the issue; wording\nreview pass.\n\n## Dependencies\n\n01, 02 (scanning stack must exist to verify).\n\n## Non-goals\n\nChanging GitHub org/repo settings (owner-only), bug bounty program, cosign\nsigning implementation (roadmap note only), pentest engagement.\n\n## Design References\n\nDESIGN.md §9 (esp. §9.1, §9.8, §9.10–§9.11); ADR-002, ADR-005;\nISSUE_PLAN §1.\n\n---\n_Derived from [`docs/issues/34-security-policy.md`](https://github.com/Saber5656/openintercom/blob/main/docs/issues/34-security-policy.md) — the repo doc is canonical; update it first if this issue drifts. Design references: [`docs/DESIGN.md`](https://github.com/Saber5656/openintercom/blob/main/docs/DESIGN.md), plan: [`docs/ISSUE_PLAN.md`](https://github.com/Saber5656/openintercom/blob/main/docs/ISSUE_PLAN.md)._\n","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Saber5656/openintercom/issues/35/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Saber5656/openintercom/issues/35/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null,"pinned_comment":null,"score":1.0},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clowlove/Hermes-House/issues/647","repository_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clowlove/Hermes-House","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clowlove/Hermes-House/issues/647/labels{/name}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clowlove/Hermes-House/issues/647/comments","events_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/clowlove/Hermes-House/issues/647/events","html_url":"https://github.com/clowlove/Hermes-House/issues/647","id":4819858218,"node_id":"I_kwDOSTDWf88AAAABH0kzKg","number":647,"title":"⭐ 发现趋势项目: airecon (786⭐)","user":{"login":"clowlove","id":278654616,"node_id":"U_kgDOEJvumA","avatar_url":"https://avat